From: Gentoo mjmap maintainers
Subject: Use the system mjmap configuration as the final fallback

Preserve the command-line and environment overrides while making the
distribution-provided private configuration the default.  Keep the path in a
string variable so Prefix builds can set it with the Go linker's -X option.

--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -18,8 +18,8 @@ gmake -C mjmap PREFIX=~/.local
 ## Configuration
 
 mjmap uses the configuration file specified by `-c` or `--config`. If the
-option is omitted, it uses the path in `$MJMAP_CONFIG` when set, then falls
-back to `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mjmap/config.scfg`.
+option is omitted, it uses the path in `$MJMAP_CONFIG` when set, then falls
+back to `/etc/mail/mjmap`.
 
 The configuration file is very short:
 
